From 692f9c2592ebf035428a06fd26c81ead0b5edae6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:57:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Gate worker execution on config completeness (Phase 1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extends the existing product-onboarding gate down to per-worker field
completeness: inngest/skill.ts's execute-skill-run function previously
only checked the boolean "enabled" flag before running a scheduled,
webhook-triggered, or chat-triggered skill, with no awareness of whether
the worker's own required config was actually filled in. A worker armed
with blank required fields would silently run anyway on every future
cron or webhook.

Adds worker-config-completeness.ts with real, verified checkers for
pile-on, win-back, leak-map, and pre-call-read, each checked against the
actual EngagementStack columns (schema.ts) rather than guessed field
names, including conditional requirements (e.g. an SMS credential only
blocks once a non-"none" SMS platform is chosen). Several fields already
have safe, documented defaults in the schema itself and are deliberately
excluded from blocking.

On missing fields, the run throws into the existing failRun() path,
which already fires a critical-severity Slack/in-app notification via
notifyRunOutcome — no new notification plumbing needed.

Scope: pin-down, Reputation Manager, Cold Open, and the remaining Whop
workers are not covered by this pass. The dispatcher fails safe (no
checker registered = nothing blocks) rather than guessing at unverified
field mappings for those.

