Adds real checkers for pin-down (12 blocking fields, verified against
EngagementStack/offerDetails — castingChoice and prospectMeets excluded
after finding script-builder.ts documents both already falling back to
"founder_on_camera" when unset; publishDomain excluded as functionally
dead code, confirmed via repo-wide grep), rep-onboarding (existence of a
repIdentityGraphs row — soleAuthorityName is DB NOT NULL so a row
existing already implies it's set), the 5 Cold Open workers with real
fields, and 3 Whop workers (whop-connect, whop-cancellation-save-offer,
whop-bridge-manager).

Milestone finding: Cold Open's workers already self-guard their own
config at the top of execute() (runIcpLock, runVoiceCapture, etc. each
throw their own clear error through the same failRun() path) — verified
by reading all 5 service files. This was not an open hole the way
pile-on/win-back/leak-map were; what this pass adds there is consistency
(one MissingField shape across every product) and catching it before the
worker's own step.run overhead, not closing a raw gap. Documented
accurately in the module header rather than overclaimed.

whop-cancellation-save-offer's minTenureDays/cooldownDays are excluded
from blocking — schema.ts documents real defaults (30/90) for both.
discount/duration/message have no such default ("unset means nothing to
propose yet, not propose with a guessed discount" per the schema's own
comment) and do block.

Typecheck: 0 new errors (5 pre-existing, unrelated to this work, in test
files — confirmed identical with git stash). Test suite: identical 59
pre-existing failures before and after (environment/DB-related, not
caused by this change).

Still not covered: the remaining 12 Whop workers verified zero-config in
the plan doc need no checker (there's nothing to check). Reputation
Manager's other 6 workers need nothing beyond rep-onboarding, same
reasoning. Genuinely complete for every worker that has real,
storage-backed fields to check.

